    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Almost 140 year history of the Sacred Heart church",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The church of the Sacred Heart was consecrated by Bishop John Butt on 17 June 1887, the Feast of the Sacred Heart.  This date was just three days before the 50th anniversary of Queen Victoria ascending to the throne. The church was designed by renowned church architect, Frederick Walters, in the Decorated Gothic style with seven altars, 19 saints' statues and an impressive rood overhead.  The parish was run by the Jesuit order of priests until it was handed over the the Archdiocese of Southwark at an historic concelebrated Mass on Sunday 10 January 2014."
            ]
        }
